<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Craigellachie, British Columbia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Craigellachie is a place in Eagle Pass in the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, where the last spike of the Canadian Pacific Railway was driven on 7 November 1885. The ceremony, performed by the railway's director Donald Smith, completed the line from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> to the Pacific and fulfilled the promise that had brought British Columbia into Confederation in 1871.</p></div>
